{"name":"Rooftop Garden","hex":"#9ead92","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rooftop","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The area atop a roof.","The top layer of a roof; the material covering or composing a roof."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rooftop"},{"term":"garden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An outdoor area containing one or more types of plants, usually plants grown for food or ornamental purposes.","Such an ornamental place to which the public have access."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To grow plants in a garden; to create or maintain a garden.","Of a batsman, to inspect and tap the pitch lightly with the bat so as to smooth out small rough patches and irregularities."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/garden"}],"entries":[{"title":"Roof garden","blocks":[{"text":"A roof garden is a garden on the roof of a building. Besides the decorative benefit, roof plantings may provide food, temperature control, hydrological benefits, architectural enhancement, habitats or corridors for wildlife, recreational opportunities, and in large scale it may even have ecological benefits. The practice of cultivating food on the rooftop of buildings is sometimes referred to as rooftop farming. Rooftop farming is usually done using green roof, hydroponics, aeroponics or air-dynaponics systems or container gardens."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/30_Rockefeller_Center_rooftop.jpg/330px-30_Rockefeller_Center_rooftop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roof_garden"},{"title":"Roof","blocks":[{"text":"A roof is the top covering of a building, including all materials and constructions necessary to support it on the walls of the building or on uprights, providing protection against rain, snow, sunlight, extremes of temperature, and wind. A roof is part of the building envelope."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Tak_-_Ystad-2022.jpg/330px-Tak_-_Ystad-2022.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roof"},{"title":"Garden","blocks":[{"text":"A garden is a planned space, usually outdoors, set aside for the cultivation, display, and enjoyment of plants and other forms of nature. The single feature identifying even the wildest wild garden is control. The garden can incorporate both natural and artificial materials."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg/330px-Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garden"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/The_Sky_Garden.jpg/500px-The_Sky_Garden.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/The_Sky_Garden.jpg/1280px-The_Sky_Garden.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/The_Sky_Garden.jpg/500px-The_Sky_Garden.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" Sky garden at 20 Fenchurch Street in the historic City of London financial district","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Sky_Garden.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/DirkvdM_casa_grande_roof_terrace.jpg/500px-DirkvdM_casa_grande_roof_terrace.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/DirkvdM_casa_grande_roof_terrace.jpg/1280px-DirkvdM_casa_grande_roof_terrace.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.or